<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rahmon Nabiyev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1930–1993</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rahmon Nabiyev was first secretary of the Communist Party of the Tajik SSR from 1982 to 1985. Returning to power in 1991, he was elected the first president of independent Tajikistan, but rising conflict between his supporters and an Islamist-democratic opposition turned into civil war, and he was forced to resign in September 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rahmon-nabiyev.jpg" alt="Rahmon Nabiyev" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EgemenMedia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rahmon_Nabiyev_1991-1992_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
